cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the versioned software release."
title: "Genuine Zero Uniform Atlas Energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Massensini
    given-names: Thiago
license: MIT
version: 0.16.0
date-released: 2026-08-20
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the native real-camera/Genuine zero identity, the
  faithful C2--C7 cutoff operator, exact critical cutoff-tail jets, and the
  finite-to-limit transverse-energy architecture. Version 0.16.0 closes the
  concrete finite microscopic-positivity gate at every presented critical
  simple zero. It derives fixed inverse-cutoff corrected and raw first-jet
  bounds, eventual positive floors for both clock Gram scalars and the temporal
  Schur denominator, a corrected finite-energy floor, fixed non-jet residual,
  pairing, and radial-gradient channels, and an eventual lower bound by half
  of the exact phase floor. The release preserves the distinction between
  cutoff M and analytic multiplicity m: the quadratic theorem is the m=1
  sector. Arbitrary-multiplicity near-axis transport, compact-complement
  nonvanishing, exact regional coverage, and a global strip-wide certificate
  remain outside the promoted claim.
